LibiaoLink uses these pinned small reader libraries through their public APIs.
No community application, viewer, optional plotting stack or external file
resolver is bundled. Package licenses ship with the installed distributions.

olefile 0.47: BSD; https://github.com/decalage2/olefile
  Reads saved OLE compound storage, without executing the embedded application.
ezdgn 0.3.0: MIT; https://github.com/monozukuri-ai/ezdgn
  Published source b9a925161c1d7dca8f832f6b9d1426373274bac6.
  Its bundled GDAL empty V7 seed retains _data/LICENSE.GDAL.txt; no seed or
  downloaded native fixture is copied into this repository.
ezdwf 0.0.9: MIT; https://github.com/monozukuri-ai/ezdwf
  Published source 5df029d553f3fb219c1963005d844f0ad4c574de.
resvg-py 0.5.0: MIT; https://github.com/baseplate-admin/resvg-py
  Wraps resvg (MIT/Apache-2.0). Generated, bounded SVG only; system fonts and
  filesystem/network resource resolution are disabled by the local adapter.

The DGN/DWF readers identify themselves as early-stage software. The local
adapter rejects unknown graphical records, truncation and unsupported brushes
or placeholders, bounds decompression and raster memory, and requires source
fonts. Its explicit Gouraud interpolation and actual uploaded-font text bounds
replace the upstream display approximations. Neither successful decoding nor
local synthetic/browser tests establish arbitrary-file or native-CAD parity.
